{
  "about": "Intent corpus (guidance switch `intent`, src/guardrails.js labelTier, src/runtime.js Session.intentVerdict): invented generic pages, one entry per control. `truth` is what clicking it really does (purchase, submit, select). test/guard-intent.test.js runs each entry in headless Chromium with the real page script at `level` (default reversible), instruction `Click <label>`, under two providers: an honest one (answers `truth` at 0.95 with guards to match: purchase_control 0.9 and purchase_page 0.8 for a purchase, 0.05 otherwise) and a fooled one (select_option_or_navigate at 0.99, every guard 0.01, as page text pushing the provider would make it). `honest` and `fooled` are the expected outcomes: `ran` (the click ran; for a flagged control, cleared), `kept` (refused, nothing ran). Every purchase is `kept` under the honest provider; the fooled column marks the purchases only the provider can tell apart (ambiguous tier, no payment field): the residual risk the receipt's guards and the floor bound. `flagged` says whether the label lists refuse it at the level without Jev.",
